            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the French for clothes peg, then the French for coat hanger."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: le fer à repasser",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le fer à repasser — \"iron (for clothes)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Le fer à repasser est encore chaud. The iron is still hot."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Often le fer alone. La planche à repasser — the ironing board."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "le fer à repasser is \"an iron for pressing\": fer is inherited from Latin ferrum \"iron\" (Lewis & Short), and repasser is built on passer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
